@startuml seq-06-anomaly-detection-pipeline
title Anomaly Detection — Full Pipeline (Rule-Based + Z-Score)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
autonumber

actor "Security Analyst\n(Angular)" as SA
participant "Gateway\n:9000" as GW
participant "Anomaly Detection\nService :9003" as ADS
participant "AnomalyEngine\n(z-score)" as Engine
participant "AnomalyStore\n(in-memory)" as Store
participant "AnomalyService\n(Angular)" as FE_SVC
participant "Security\nDashboard" as Dashboard
participant "Loki :3100" as Loki
participant "Grafana\nD4 :3000" as Grafana

== Simulate Attack (frontend button) ==

SA -> GW : POST /api/anomaly/simulate/registration-flood\nBearer JWT (SECURITY_ANALYST)
GW -> ADS : lb://anomaly-detection-service
ADS -> Engine : detectRegistrationFlood()
Engine -> Engine : compute rate (events/s)\ncompare vs DR-001 threshold (20/s)\ncompute z-score against rolling window

alt Rate exceeds threshold
  Engine -> Store : append AnomalyEvent {\n  type: REGISTRATION_FLOOD,\n  severity: HIGH,\n  zscore: 3.4,\n  rate: 28.2 }
  ADS -> Loki : log "[ANOMALY] type=REGISTRATION_FLOOD sev=HIGH rate=28.2"
  ADS --> GW : 200 { injected: 1 }
else Below threshold
  ADS --> GW : 200 { injected: 0 }
end

== Frontend Polling (5s interval) ==

FE_SVC -> GW : GET /api/anomaly/events?limit=50\nBearer JWT
note right of FE_SVC : EventSource not used — can't send Bearer header\nHTTP polling with interval(5000) + switchMap
GW -> ADS : lb://anomaly-detection-service
ADS -> Store : query(null, null, 50)
Store --> ADS : List<AnomalyEvent> (newest first)
ADS --> FE_SVC : 200 [ { id, timestamp, type, severity, zscore, rate, imsi } ]

FE_SVC -> Dashboard : signal events.set(…)
Dashboard -> Dashboard : recompute:\nthreatLevel (quiet/medium/high/critical)\nseveritySlices, typeCounts, rateHistory

== Grafana observability ==

Loki -> Grafana : stream {app="anomaly-detection-service"} |= "[ANOMALY]"
Grafana -> Grafana : D4 panels:\n- CRITICAL/HIGH/MEDIUM count\n- events-per-minute timeseries\n- severity donut chart

@enduml
